            <ArticleTitle>Age UK enlists nurses to tackle loneliness in older people.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7748/nop.29.1.6.s2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A pilot programme by charity Age UK has helped to combat loneliness in older people, early findings show. The scheme, involving eight local Age UK services in England, raises awareness of the common characteristics of loneliness among ward nurses, hospital discharge teams and practice nurses.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
